window.HDH_SEARCH=[{"t":"Getting started","s":"","u":"docs/getting-started/","x":"FixPin turns \"the button doesn't work\" into a screenshot with the broken spot marked, a note, and a private link that deletes itself. No account, no password. !FixPin in four steps: point at the broken button, add a note, share the private link, and it deletes itself."},{"t":"Getting started","s":"Two ways to use it","u":"docs/getting-started/#two-ways-to-use-it","x":"- The app works on any phone, tablet or computer. Open it, add a screenshot, mark the problem, get a link. Nothing to install. - The browser extension works on a computer. It takes the screenshot of the page for you and adds the page address, your screen size and browser, and any errors from the page. Both give you the same report page, and both are free."},{"t":"Getting started","s":"Your first report (the app)","u":"docs/getting-started/#your-first-report-the-app","x":"1. Open the FixPin app and choose, drop or paste a screenshot. On a phone, take a screenshot and share it to FixPin once the app is installed. !The FixPin start screen with a box to choose, drop or paste a screenshot. 2. Click or drag a box around each problem (up to 5). Click a box again to remove it. 3. Write what is wrong. Add the page address if you know it. !A screenshot of a bakery order page with two numbered red boxes: the Place your order button and the price. 4. Choose how long the link works (1, 7 or 30 days) and, if you like, a passcode. 5. Press Create link , then Copy link and se"},{"t":"Getting started","s":"Install the app","u":"docs/getting-started/#install-the-app","x":"On a computer, use your browser's install button in the address bar (Chrome, Edge). On iPhone, use Share → Add to Home Screen . On Android, use the menu → Install app . Once installed it opens like any other app and appears in your phone's share sheet."},{"t":"Getting started","s":"Using WordPress?","u":"docs/getting-started/#using-wordpress","x":"Fixpass adds one thing FixPin deliberately does not do: it gives your support team safe, temporary administrator access to a WordPress site, with no password shared."},{"t":"The browser extension","s":"","u":"docs/extension/","x":"The extension works in Chrome, Edge, Brave and Firefox."},{"t":"The browser extension","s":"Install","u":"docs/extension/#install","x":"Until it is listed in the browser stores, install it from the latest release or from the source: - Chrome, Edge, Brave: open chrome://extensions , turn on Developer mode , choose Load unpacked and pick the extension folder. - Firefox: open about:debugging , choose This Firefox , then Load Temporary Add-on and pick manifest.json . !The extension in action: click the toolbar button, click the broken button, press Send, and the link is copied."},{"t":"The browser extension","s":"Use it","u":"docs/extension/#use-it","x":"1. Go to the page with the problem. 2. Click the FixPin button, or press Alt+Shift+F . 3. If the problem needs a click to appear, reproduce it now. 4. Click the problem, or drag a box around it. Add up to 5 spots. 5. Write a note, choose how long the link lasts, and press Send . The link is copied. !The FixPin overlay on a web page: two numbered red boxes around the broken button and price, and a panel to add a note and send."},{"t":"The browser extension","s":"What comes with a report","u":"docs/extension/#what-comes-with-a-report","x":"The screenshot, your spots (with the page element each one is on), the page address and title, your screen size and browser, and any errors that happened after you clicked the button: JavaScript errors, failed requests, and console errors and warnings."},{"t":"The browser extension","s":"What the extension can see","u":"docs/extension/#what-the-extension-can-see","x":"It only runs on the page you click it on (the activeTab permission). It does not read pages in the background, has no analytics, and sends nothing until you press Send . It can't run on browser pages (such as chrome:// ) or on the extension stores."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"","u":"docs/sharing/","x":""},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"The link","u":"docs/sharing/#the-link","x":"Every report has its own link, made of a random 192-bit code that can't be guessed. Anyone who has the link can open the report, so share it only with the people helping you."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"How long it lasts","u":"docs/sharing/#how-long-it-lasts","x":"You choose 1, 7 or 30 days. After that the report and its screenshot are deleted automatically."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"Passcode","u":"docs/sharing/#passcode","x":"Add a passcode to ask for one before the report opens. Tell the person the passcode separately from the link (a different message is best)."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"Delete it early","u":"docs/sharing/#delete-it-early","x":"Open the report on the device that created it and press Delete now . It is gone for everyone who had the link."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"What the report page shows","u":"docs/sharing/#what-the-report-page-shows","x":"!The report page: the screenshot with numbered spots, the note, and details such as the page, screen size and browser. The screenshot with your numbered spots, your note, the page address, screen size and browser, any errors the extension collected, and a Copy details button that formats everything as plain text for an email or ticket."},{"t":"Sharing a report","s":"Size limit","u":"docs/sharing/#size-limit","x":"A report can be up to 2 MB. The app shrinks large screenshots for you."},{"t":"Privacy","s":"","u":"docs/privacy/","x":"- No accounts, no tracking, no cookies. The app and the extension have no analytics. This website counts visits anonymously, with no cookies and no personal data. - Stored: only what you send (screenshot, note, page address, browser and screen size, page errors from the extension), under a random 192-bit link. - Kept 1, 7 or 30 days as you choose, then deleted automatically (Cloudflare KV expiry). The device that made a report can delete it earlier. - A passcode is stored only as a salted SHA-256 hash. - Anyone with the link (and passcode) can see the report. Do not include passwords or card n"},{"t":"FAQ","s":"","u":"docs/faq/","x":""},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Do I need an account?","u":"docs/faq/#do-i-need-an-account","x":"No. There are no accounts. Reports are private links that expire."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Is it free?","u":"docs/faq/#is-it-free","x":"Yes. FixPin is free and open source (GPL)."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Who can see my report?","u":"docs/faq/#who-can-see-my-report","x":"Anyone with the link, and the passcode if you set one. Nobody else: reports are not listed or searchable."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"What if my screenshot shows private information?","u":"docs/faq/#what-if-my-screenshot-shows-private-information","x":"Hide it before you send. The app and the extension send exactly the screenshot you see, nothing more. Don't include passwords or card numbers."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Does FixPin give support access to my site?","u":"docs/faq/#does-fixpin-give-support-access-to-my-site","x":"No. FixPin only shows the problem. For WordPress sites, Fixpass adds safe, temporary administrator access."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Does it work offline?","u":"docs/faq/#does-it-work-offline","x":"The app opens offline, but creating and opening reports needs a connection, because reports live on the server until they expire."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Can I run my own server?","u":"docs/faq/#can-i-run-my-own-server","x":"Yes. See Host your own FixPin."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Which browsers does the extension support?","u":"docs/faq/#which-browsers-does-the-extension-support","x":"Chrome, Edge, Brave and Firefox."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Why were no errors collected?","u":"docs/faq/#why-were-no-errors-collected","x":"The extension collects errors from the moment you click its button. Click it first, then reproduce the problem."},{"t":"Host your own FixPin","s":"","u":"docs/self-hosting/","x":"You need a free Cloudflare account. bash npm install npx wrangler login npx wrangler kv namespace create REPORTS paste the id into wrangler.toml npm test npm run deploy Then set DEFAULT SERVER in the extension ( src/config.js ) to your Worker's address. Limits: reports up to 2 MB, links 1/7/30 days. For heavy public use, add a Cloudflare rate-limiting rule on POST /api/reports ."},{"t":"Developers","s":"","u":"docs/developers/","x":"FixPin is two repositories: - fixpin: the app ( pwa/ ), the Cloudflare Worker ( worker/ ) and this website ( website/ ). - fixpin-extension: the browser extension."},{"t":"Developers","s":"The API","u":"docs/developers/#the-api","x":"Method Path What it does POST /api/reports Create a report. Returns id , ownerToken , expiresAt . GET /api/reports/:id Read a report. Send the X-Passcode header if it has one. DELETE /api/reports/:id Delete early. Needs the X-Owner-Token header. A report is JSON: url , title , note , ua , viewport ( w , h , dpr ), spots ( x , y , w , h as fractions 0 to 1 of the screenshot, plus selector and note ), errors ( type , msg ), screenshot (a PNG, JPEG or WebP data URL), days (1, 7 or 30) and an optional passcode . The server keeps only the fields it knows, at sane sizes, and only accepts images as s"},{"t":"Developers","s":"Storage","u":"docs/developers/#storage","x":"Cloudflare KV with a time-to-live equal to the expiry, so deletion needs no job. The owner token and passcode are stored only as SHA-256 hashes."},{"t":"Developers","s":"Develop","u":"docs/developers/#develop","x":"bash npm install npm test npm run dev"}];